<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  network_security_config.xml (debug) - VoltShare Mobile

  This file replaces the one in src/main for debug builds only. Android merges
  resources per build variant, and a file of the same name in the variant's
  source set takes precedence over the one in main.

  Why it exists: the address of the Web API is now read from local.properties,
  so each member of the team builds against their own machine. The list of
  permitted cleartext hosts in src/main cannot know those addresses, and an
  address missing from it fails at runtime with a cleartext error that gives no
  hint as to the cause. Permitting cleartext generally in the debug build
  removes that trap.

  The release build is unaffected: it still uses the narrow list in
  src/main/res/xml, so the shipped application only ever sends plain HTTP to
  the addresses named there.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
